# 13. Design Decisions and Rationale

## 13.1 Console-Based Interface

A console interface was selected because the project focuses on Java programming concepts rather than GUI development.

It also keeps the project simple and allows the main functionality to be implemented using core Java.

## 13.2 ArrayList

ArrayList was used to store patients, doctors, appointments, records, rooms, bills, and staff.

It provides a simple way to store multiple objects and add or remove records during program execution.

## 13.3 Separate Classes

Separate classes were created for important entities such as Patient, Doctor, Appointment, MedicalRecord, Room, Bill, and Staff.

This makes the relationship between the real-world hospital entities and Java objects easier to understand.

## 13.4 Menu-Based Navigation

A main menu and individual submenus were used so the user can easily select the required operation.

## 13.5 Input Validation

Validation was included to prevent common input errors such as invalid age, incorrect phone numbers, negative charges, invalid dates, and invalid menu choices.

## 13.6 Java Standard Library

Only standard Java libraries are used. This keeps the project easy to compile and run without requiring additional software or external dependencies.

