# 19. Challenges Faced

During development, some challenges were faced while connecting the different modules.

One challenge was maintaining different types of information such as patients, doctors, appointments, and bills without using a database.

Another challenge was validating user input. Since the program takes information directly from the console, incorrect values could cause problems if they were not handled properly.

Appointment management also required additional checking so that the same doctor could not be booked for two appointments on the same date.

Calculating the total bill was another part where the different charges had to be combined correctly.

Handling these problems helped in understanding how different Java concepts can work together in a single project.

