# 22. Conclusion

The Hospital Management System successfully demonstrates how Java programming can be used to solve a practical management problem.

The application provides different modules for managing patients, doctors, appointments, medical records, rooms, billing, and staff.

The project uses core Java concepts such as classes, objects, methods, ArrayList, loops, conditional statements, exception handling, input validation, and date handling.

Testing showed that the main functions work correctly with both valid and invalid inputs.

Although the current project is a console-based application without permanent database storage, it provides a basic foundation that can be expanded with additional features in the future.

Overall, the project demonstrates the practical application of Java programming concepts in building a functional management system.

